        "heading_WKaVpK": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "sub_heading": "",
            "heading": "Common Types of Custom Adhesive Tapes",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "rich_text_cstm": "<p>Custom adhesive tapes are varied to suit their diverse applications. A range of materials are available, from simple paper to sturdy vinyl, with options to suit diverse functional and aesthetic requirements. Some of the most common types of custom adhesive tape include the following:</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_4Uk8Y7": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Paper Tapes",
            "content": "<p>Paper tapes are among the most common and the most versatile, typically used for sealing, marking, labeling, and masking. Their popularity comes from their low cost combined with their ease of customization. Most paper tapes are easy to print on, with options for both matte and glossy finishes. Similarly, in terms of function, different papers enable varying degrees of strength, removability, and temperature resistance, so paper tapes can conform to diverse application requirements. <br/></p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_DJWjFG": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Foil Tapes",
            "content": "<p>Foil tapes are durable with adhesives that can withstand exposure to harsh outdoor or industrial environments. The most common types of foil tape combine aluminum or copper foil (which may be either conductive or non-conductive) with a flexible adhesive backing. More specialized applications may call instead for lead or stainless steel foil. As a category, foil tapes tend to offer superior strength while conforming to irregular surfaces, making them an ideal choice for shielding or sealing electronics.<br/><br/></p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_3iqk6X": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Mylar Tapes",
            "content": "<p>Mylar tapes are ideal for tough surfaces like heavy-duty industrial equipment. They create a strong, stable seal that can handle vibrations, temperature changes, and other stresses. Some of our Mylar tapes also feature a brushed silver polyester layer, giving them a smooth, attractive finish that looks great on equipment.<br/><br/></p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_RfgVgr": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Vinyl Tapes",
            "content": "<p>Vinyl tapes are a common choice for labeling and striping, as well as for various OSHA applications. These tapes are available in vibrant colors for high visibility, with options for custom graphics and instructions when required. Functionally, vinyl tapes resist heat, corrosion, and moisture, so they have the lasting power needed for critical safety applications.<br/><br/></p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
